HST Office on Windows: own file-type ProgIDs and UNO install-path key, so it does not take over LibreOffice's.

The MSI registered LibreOffice's ProgID names (LibreOffice.WriterDocument.1, LibreOffice.Docx, ...)
and wrote HKLM\Software\LibreOffice\UNO\InstallPath. With both suites installed, the one installed
last owned the other's open commands and install path, and uninstalling either deleted the keys the
other relied on.

- scp2: every file-type ProgID is HSTOffice.<name> (keys, CurVer, OpenWithProgids, conditional .ext
  defaults, the Capabilities FileAssociations/MimeAssociations behind RegisteredApplications).
  The AppUserModelIDs and the OLE class IDs are unchanged.
- The UNO install path is HKLM\Software\HASON TECH\HST Office\UNO\InstallPath; every reader in the
  tree (cppuhelper findsofficepath, cli_ure native bootstrap, the Windows default-app check) reads it.
  The disabled ODK loaders are not changed.
- LookForRegisteredExtensions takes a Microsoft Office format only when no application, WordPad or
  HST Office itself owns it; a LibreOffice.* default now belongs to LibreOffice. The saved previous
  association is HSTBackupAssociation(Deref), separate from LibreOffice's LOBackupAssociation.
- The default-app check and the shell extension's self-registration table use the HST ProgIDs.
- Unchanged on purpose: OLE storage type names written into documents (embedserv, msfilter, oox).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

